IMPORT prelude

-- Coroners Act 1996 (Western Australia) -- a death in the family: whether the death is a "Western Australian death" and a
-- "reportable death" (s 3, s 3A, s 3B), who must report it, to whom, and the penalty (ss 17, 18), whether the coroner will
-- investigate (s 19, s 19A), whether an inquest must be held (ss 22, 23) and the family's right to ask for one (s 24), who
-- is the senior next of kin (s 37(5)) and what the family must be told and allowed (ss 20, 25(4), 26A, 30(2), 35), the
-- family's objection to a post mortem (s 37), and when the body is released (ss 29, 30, 36(3)).
--
-- SEAT: the family of the deceased. Every decision is phrased as a member of the family would ask it: "Must this death be
-- reported to the coroner?", "Must I report it, and to whom?", "Will there be an inquest?", "May I ask for one?", "Am I the
-- senior next of kin?", "Can the post mortem go ahead despite my objection?", "When will we get the body back?". Most of
-- the Act addresses the coroner, the State Coroner, doctors and carers; what it means for the family is what must be done,
-- what they must be told, what they may ask for, and by when. Where the Act hands a judgment to the coroner ("appears to the
-- coroner", "believes", "determines"), the State Coroner, the Attorney General or the Supreme Court, that judgment is asked
-- as a fact, never guessed. Fields and parameters marked (coroner) are such judgments.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3 ("reportable death", "Western Australian death", "person held in care" asked as a fact), s 3A,
-- s 3B, s 17(1), (3), (4), (5), s 18(1), s 19(1), s 19A(1)-(3), s 20(1), s 22, s 23(2), s 24, s 25(4), s 26A, s 29(1)-(3),
-- s 30, s 35, s 36(3) (as it bears on s 29), s 37(1)-(5), s 44(1)-(3); Coroners Regulations 1997 regs 15, 17, 22, 22A, 23B
-- and Schedule 3 item 2 (what the family pays for a copy of the record of investigation).
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 47642, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47642.txt; its compilation table runs to the Aboriginal Heritage Legislation Amendment
-- and Repeal Act 2023 s 27 (in force 15 November 2023); the State Superannuation (Transitional and Consequential Provisions)
-- Act 2000 s 36(2) is listed as uncommenced and is not reflected. Regulations used: the Coroners Regulations 1997, version
-- 03-v0-00 in force from 1 July 2026 (legislation.wa.gov.au law_s4371), as deposited at
-- ../../../coroners-regulations-1997/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49623.txt (retrieved 21 October 2026). They prescribe NO
-- circumstances for s 3 limb (d) or s 22(1)(f), and do not vary the s 37(5) order of next of kin ("unless otherwise
-- prescribed"): none of regs 1-25 or the Schedules does. Those two limbs therefore add nothing and are left out, and the
-- s 37(5) list applies as written. Used from them: reg 15 (a s 24 request in writing with reasons), reg 17 (the prescribed
-- list of interested persons for s 44(3)), and regs 22, 22A and 23B with Schedule 3 item 2 (the fee for a copy of the record
-- of investigation).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the court, the State Coroner and other officers (Part 2: ss 5-16); s 19(2), s 21, s 25(1)-(3), (5), ss 26,
-- 27, 28 (notification to the Registrar; noted only); s 31; powers of investigation (ss 32, 33), the post mortem itself and
-- tissue removal (s 34), s 36 beyond its effect on the disposal certificate, exhumation (s 38); the conduct of inquests
-- (Part 5: ss 39-53, except s 44(1)-(3)); Part 6 (ss 53A-59); s 62. The meaning of "person held in care" (s 3, eleven
-- statutory categories borrowed from other Acts) is asked as a fact.
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the family of the deceased, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice.

§ `Coroners Act 1996 (WA) -- a death in the family`

§§ `the facts about the death`

-- s 3 "Western Australian death means a death -- (a) that occurred in Western Australia; or (b) where the body is in Western
-- Australia; or (c) the cause of which occurred in Western Australia; or (d) of a person who was ordinarily residing in
-- Western Australia at the time of death; or (e) of a person who, at the time of death, was in an industry to and in
-- relation to which the Industrial Relations Act 1979 applies due to the operation of section 3 of that Act."
-- s 3 "reportable death means a Western Australian death -- (a) that appears to have been unexpected, unnatural or violent
-- or to have resulted, directly or indirectly, from injury; or (b) that occurs during an anaesthetic; or (c) that occurs as
-- a result of an anaesthetic and is not due to natural causes; or (d) that occurs in prescribed circumstances; or (e) of a
-- person who immediately before death was a person held in care; or (f) that appears to have been caused or contributed to
-- while the person was held in care; or (g) that appears to have been caused or contributed to by any action of a member of
-- the Police Force; or (h) of a person whose identity is unknown; or (i) that occurs in Western Australia where the cause of
-- death has not been certified under section 44 of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998; or (j) that
-- occurred outside Western Australia where the cause of death is not certified to by a person who, under the law in force
-- in that place, is a legally qualified medical practitioner".
-- Limb (a) is split into its three parts because s 19A turns on "unexpected" alone.
-- Limb (i) is read as asking whether a doctor has certified OR WILL certify under s 44 (which allows 48 hours): read
-- literally, every death in WA is reportable from the moment of death until the certificate is signed (an inference; see
-- NOTES.md).
-- "Person held in care" (s 3: wards of the CEO, prisoners, people in police custody, involuntary mental health patients,
-- detained young offenders and others) is asked as a fact. Limb (d), "prescribed circumstances": the Coroners Regulations
-- 1997 prescribe none, so the limb is left out.
DECLARE Death HAS
    `occurred in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body is in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cause occurred in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deceased ordinarily resided in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deceased was in an industry under the Industrial Relations Act 1979 s 3` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appears to have been unexpected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appears to have been unnatural or violent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appears to have resulted, directly or indirectly, from injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `occurred during an anaesthetic` IS A BOOLEAN
    `occurred as a result of an anaesthetic and not due to natural causes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deceased was a person held in care immediately before death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appears caused or contributed to while the deceased was held in care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appears caused or contributed to by an action of a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the identity of the deceased is unknown` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a doctor has certified, or will certify, the cause under BDM Act s 44` IS A BOOLEAN
    `outside WA, the cause is certified by a legally qualified medical practitioner there` IS A BOOLEAN
    `followed a voluntary assisted dying substance under the VAD Act 2019` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a child born alive after a lawful abortion, who died following it` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `3, 3A, 3B -- must this death be reported to the coroner`

@export Is this a Western Australian death, under the Coroners Act 1996 (WA) s 3?
GIVEN `the death` IS A Death @desc Where the death, its cause and the body were, and where the deceased lived and worked
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a Western Australian death` `the death` IF
        `the death`'s `occurred in Western Australia`
    OR  `the death`'s `the body is in Western Australia`
    OR  `the death`'s `the cause occurred in Western Australia`
    OR  `the death`'s `the deceased ordinarily resided in Western Australia`
    OR  `the death`'s `the deceased was in an industry under the Industrial Relations Act 1979 s 3`

-- The limbs (a)-(j) of "reportable death", before the exceptions in ss 3A and 3B. Limb (d) (prescribed circumstances) is
-- absent: the Coroners Regulations 1997 prescribe none.
GIVEN `the death` IS A Death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a limb of reportable death other than unexpected applies` `the death` IF
        `the death`'s `appears to have been unnatural or violent`
    OR  `the death`'s `appears to have resulted, directly or indirectly, from injury`
    OR  `the death`'s `occurred during an anaesthetic`
    OR  `the death`'s `occurred as a result of an anaesthetic and not due to natural causes`
    OR  `the death`'s `the deceased was a person held in care immediately before death`
    OR  `the death`'s `appears caused or contributed to while the deceased was held in care`
    OR  `the death`'s `appears caused or contributed to by an action of a police officer`
    OR  `the death`'s `the identity of the deceased is unknown`
    OR  (`the death`'s `occurred in Western Australia` AND (NOT `the death`'s `a doctor has certified, or will certify, the cause under BDM Act s 44`))
    OR  ((NOT `the death`'s `occurred in Western Australia`) AND (NOT `the death`'s `outside WA, the cause is certified by a legally qualified medical practitioner there`))

-- s 3A(1): a death after a voluntary assisted dying substance under the VAD Act 2019 "is not a reportable death"; (2): "does
-- not apply to a Western Australian death of a person who immediately before death was a person held in care".
-- s 3B(1): not a reportable death where "(a) an abortion is performed on a person; (b) the child is born alive and
-- subsequently dies following the performance of the abortion; (c) ... the performance of the abortion does not constitute
-- an offence under a written law".
GIVEN `the death` IS A Death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exception in section 3A or 3B applies` `the death` IF
        (    `the death`'s `followed a voluntary assisted dying substance under the VAD Act 2019`
         AND (NOT `the death`'s `the deceased was a person held in care immediately before death`))
    OR  `the death`'s `a child born alive after a lawful abortion, who died following it`

@export Must this death be reported to the coroner -- is it a reportable death (Coroners Act 1996 (WA) ss 3, 3A, 3B)?
GIVEN `the death` IS A Death @desc How and where the person died, whether a doctor will certify the cause, and whether they were held in care
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a reportable death` `the death` IF
        `Is this a Western Australian death` `the death`
    AND (`the death`'s `appears to have been unexpected` OR `a limb of reportable death other than unexpected applies` `the death`)
    AND (NOT `an exception in section 3A or 3B applies` `the death`)

§§ `17, 18 -- who must report it, to whom, and the penalty`

-- s 17(1): "A person must report a death that is or may be a reportable death to a coroner or a member of the Police Force
-- immediately after he or she becomes aware of the death, unless the person has reasonable grounds to believe that the
-- death has already been reported. Penalty: $1 000."
-- s 17(3): "A doctor who is present at or soon after the death of a person must report the death immediately to a coroner
-- if -- (a) the death is or may be a reportable death; or (b) the doctor is unable to determine the cause of death; or (c) in
-- the opinion of the doctor, the death has occurred under any suspicious circumstances. Penalty: $1 000."
-- s 17(4): "If more than one doctor is present ... and one of them reports it to a coroner, the other doctors need not
-- report the death but must give to the coroner investigating the death any information which may help the investigation."
-- s 17(5): the death of a person held in care "must be reported immediately to a coroner by the person under whose care the
-- deceased was held. Penalty: $1 000."
-- "Is or may be" is carried by the facts: the limbs are already framed as how the death "appears".
DECLARE `My part in the death` IS ONE OF
    `a family member or other person`
    `a doctor present at or soon after the death`
    `the person under whose care the deceased was held`

DECLARE Reporter HAS
    `my part` IS A `My part in the death`
    `I am aware of the death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have reasonable grounds to believe it has already been reported` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another doctor present has reported it to a coroner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a doctor, I cannot determine the cause of death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a doctor, I think the death occurred under suspicious circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 17(4) relieves the other doctors of s 17(3) only; s 17(1) binds them too, as it binds everyone. A doctor who knows a
-- colleague has reported to a coroner is taken to have "reasonable grounds to believe that the death has already been
-- reported" (an inference).
GIVEN `me` IS A Reporter
      `the death` IS A Death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17(1) requires me to report` `me` `the death` IF
        `me`'s `I am aware of the death`
    AND `Is this a reportable death` `the death`
    AND (NOT `me`'s `I have reasonable grounds to believe it has already been reported`)
    AND (NOT `me`'s `another doctor present has reported it to a coroner`)

GIVEN `me` IS A Reporter
      `the death` IS A Death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17(3) requires me to report` `me` `the death` IF
        `me`'s `my part` EQUALS `a doctor present at or soon after the death`
    AND (   `Is this a reportable death` `the death`
         OR `me`'s `as a doctor, I cannot determine the cause of death`
         OR `me`'s `as a doctor, I think the death occurred under suspicious circumstances`)
    AND (NOT `me`'s `another doctor present has reported it to a coroner`)

GIVEN `me` IS A Reporter
      `the death` IS A Death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17(5) requires me to report` `me` `the death` IF
        `me`'s `my part` EQUALS `the person under whose care the deceased was held`
    AND `the death`'s `the deceased was a person held in care immediately before death`

@export Must I report this death (Coroners Act 1996 (WA) s 17)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Reporter @desc Your part in the death, and whether you know it has already been reported
      `the death` IS A Death @desc How and where the person died
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I report this death` `me` `the death` IF
        `section 17(1) requires me to report` `me` `the death`
    OR  `section 17(3) requires me to report` `me` `the death`
    OR  `section 17(5) requires me to report` `me` `the death`

DECLARE `Whom I must report to` IS ONE OF
    `no one: I need not report this death`
    `a coroner or a police officer, immediately (s 17(1))`
    `a coroner, immediately (s 17(3) or (5))`

@export Whom must I report this death to, and when (Coroners Act 1996 (WA) s 17)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Reporter @desc Your part in the death, and whether you know it has already been reported
      `the death` IS A Death @desc How and where the person died
GIVETH A `Whom I must report to`
DECIDE `Whom must I report to` `me` `the death` IS
    BRANCH
      IF `section 17(3) requires me to report` `me` `the death` OR `section 17(5) requires me to report` `me` `the death`
        THEN `a coroner, immediately (s 17(3) or (5))`
      IF `section 17(1) requires me to report` `me` `the death`
        THEN `a coroner or a police officer, immediately (s 17(1))`
      OTHERWISE `no one: I need not report this death`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not reporting this death, in dollars (s 17)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Reporter @desc Your part in the death
      `the death` IS A Death @desc How and where the person died
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not reporting` `me` `the death` IS
    IF `Must I report this death` `me` `the death` THEN 1000 ELSE 0

-- s 18(1): "A person who reports a death must give to the coroner investigating the death any information which may help
-- the investigation. Penalty: $1 000." s 17(4): so must a doctor present who was relieved of reporting by another doctor.
@export Must I give the coroner any information that may help the investigation (ss 17(4), 18(1))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Reporter @desc Your part in the death
      `I reported the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reported the death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the coroner information` `me` `I reported the death` IF
        `I reported the death`
    OR  (`me`'s `my part` EQUALS `a doctor present at or soon after the death` AND `me`'s `another doctor present has reported it to a coroner`)

§§ `19, 19A -- will the coroner investigate`

-- s 19(1): "A coroner has jurisdiction to investigate a death if it appears to the coroner that the death is or may be a
-- reportable death." s 8(c): the State Coroner is "to ensure that all reportable deaths reported to a coroner are
-- investigated". s 19A(1): a coroner "is not required to investigate ... a reportable death if the coroner determines that
-- -- (a) the death is due to natural causes; and (b) the death is a reportable death solely because it appears to have been
-- unexpected"; (2) on a pathologist's written opinion; (3) not if "(a) there is a duty to hold an inquest ... or (b) the
-- death occurred during an anaesthetic".
GIVEN `the death` IS A Death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the death is reportable solely because it appears unexpected` `the death` IF
        `Is this a reportable death` `the death`
    AND `the death`'s `appears to have been unexpected`
    AND (NOT `a limb of reportable death other than unexpected applies` `the death`)

-- s 22(1) and s 23(2): when an inquest is compulsory. The directions are inputs. s 22(1)(f), "the death occurred in
-- prescribed circumstances": the Coroners Regulations 1997 prescribe none, so that paragraph is left out.
DECLARE Directions HAS
    `the Attorney General has directed an inquest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State Coroner has directed an inquest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State Coroner directed investigation of the suspected death of a missing person` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 22(1): "A coroner who has jurisdiction to investigate a death must hold an inquest if the death appears to be a Western
-- Australian death and -- (a) the deceased was immediately before death a person held in care; or (b) it appears that the
-- death was caused, or contributed to, by any action of a member of the Police Force; or (c) it appears that the death was
-- caused, or contributed to, while the deceased was a person held in care; or (d) the Attorney General so directs; or (e)
-- the State Coroner so directs; or (f) the death occurred in prescribed circumstances." s 23(2): where the State Coroner has
-- directed that a missing person's suspected death be investigated, "a coroner must hold an inquest".
GIVEN `the death` IS A Death
      `the directions` IS A Directions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a duty to hold an inquest` `the death` `the directions` IF
        `the directions`'s `the State Coroner directed investigation of the suspected death of a missing person`
    OR  (    `Is this a reportable death` `the death`
         AND (   `the death`'s `the deceased was a person held in care immediately before death`
              OR `the death`'s `appears caused or contributed to by an action of a police officer`
              OR `the death`'s `appears caused or contributed to while the deceased was held in care`
              OR `the directions`'s `the Attorney General has directed an inquest`
              OR `the directions`'s `the State Coroner has directed an inquest`))

DECLARE `Whether the coroner will investigate` IS ONE OF
    `no: it is not a reportable death, so the coroner has no jurisdiction (s 19(1))`
    `yes: the death must be investigated (ss 8(c), 19(1))`
    `the coroner need not investigate: natural causes, reportable only because unexpected (s 19A)`

@export Will the coroner investigate this death (Coroners Act 1996 (WA) ss 19, 19A)?
GIVEN `the death` IS A Death @desc How and where the person died
      `the directions` IS A Directions @desc Any direction for an inquest by the Attorney General or the State Coroner
      `the coroner has determined natural causes on a pathologist's written opinion (coroner)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the coroner, on a pathologist's written opinion, has determined that the death is due to natural causes
GIVETH A `Whether the coroner will investigate`
DECIDE `Will the coroner investigate` `the death` `the directions` `the coroner has determined natural causes on a pathologist's written opinion (coroner)` IS
    BRANCH
      IF NOT `Is this a reportable death` `the death`
        THEN `no: it is not a reportable death, so the coroner has no jurisdiction (s 19(1))`
      IF     `the coroner has determined natural causes on a pathologist's written opinion (coroner)`
         AND `the death is reportable solely because it appears unexpected` `the death`
         AND (NOT `there is a duty to hold an inquest` `the death` `the directions`)
         AND (NOT `the death`'s `occurred during an anaesthetic`)
        THEN `the coroner need not investigate: natural causes, reportable only because unexpected (s 19A)`
      OTHERWISE `yes: the death must be investigated (ss 8(c), 19(1))`

§§ `22, 23, 24 -- will there be an inquest, and may we ask for one`

DECLARE `Whether there will be an inquest` IS ONE OF
    `no: the coroner has no jurisdiction, so there can be no inquest`
    `yes: an inquest must be held (s 22(1) or s 23(2))`
    `only if the coroner thinks it desirable (s 22(2)); we may ask for one (s 24)`

@export Must an inquest be held into this death (Coroners Act 1996 (WA) ss 22, 23)?
GIVEN `the death` IS A Death @desc How and where the person died, and whether they were held in care
      `the directions` IS A Directions @desc Any direction for an inquest by the Attorney General or the State Coroner
GIVETH A `Whether there will be an inquest`
DECIDE `Must an inquest be held` `the death` `the directions` IS
    BRANCH
      IF `there is a duty to hold an inquest` `the death` `the directions`
        THEN `yes: an inquest must be held (s 22(1) or s 23(2))`
      IF `Is this a reportable death` `the death`
        THEN `only if the coroner thinks it desirable (s 22(2)); we may ask for one (s 24)`
      OTHERWISE `no: the coroner has no jurisdiction, so there can be no inquest`

-- s 24(1): "If a person asks a coroner to hold an inquest into a death which a coroner has jurisdiction to investigate, the
-- coroner may -- (a) hold an inquest ...; or (b) refuse the request and give reasons in writing for the refusal to the person
-- and to the State Coroner within a reasonable period". (1a): the request is to "(a) be made in writing; and (b) contain
-- reasons for the request". Any person may ask; the family is not singled out. Coroners Regulations 1997 reg 15 says the
-- same: the request "is to be made in writing and is to specify the reason why the inquest is sought".
@export May I ask the coroner to hold an inquest into this death (s 24(1), (1a))?
GIVEN `the death` IS A Death @desc How and where the person died
      `my request is in writing and gives reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your request is in writing and says why you want an inquest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask for an inquest` `the death` `my request is in writing and gives reasons` IF
        `Is this a reportable death` `the death`
    AND `my request is in writing and gives reasons`

-- s 24(2): "Within 7 days after receiving notice of the refusal, or if a reply to a request for an inquest to be held has
-- not been given within 3 months after the request was made, the person may apply to the Supreme Court for an order that an
-- inquest be held." (3): the Court may order one "if it is satisfied that it is necessary or desirable in the interests of
-- justice". "Within 7 days" is read as up to and including the seventh day after notice. The no-reply limb has no closing
-- date in the text.
@export May I now apply to the Supreme Court for an order that an inquest be held (s 24(2))?
GIVEN `the coroner refused my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the coroner has refused your request for an inquest
      `days since I received notice of the refusal` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since you received the coroner's notice of refusal
      `the coroner has replied to my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the coroner has replied to your request at all
      `months since I made my request` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since you made your request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the Supreme Court for an inquest` `the coroner refused my request` `days since I received notice of the refusal` `the coroner has replied to my request` `months since I made my request` IF
        (`the coroner refused my request` AND `days since I received notice of the refusal` AT MOST 7)
    OR  ((NOT `the coroner has replied to my request`) AND `months since I made my request` AT LEAST 3)

§§ `37(5) -- the senior next of kin`

-- s 37(5): "senior next of kin ... means the first person who is available from the following persons in the order of
-- priority listed -- (a) a person who, immediately before death, was living with the person and was either -- (i) legally
-- married to the person; or (ii) of or over the age of 18 years and in a marriagelike relationship ... with the person; or
-- (b) a person who, immediately before death, was legally married to the person; or (c) a son or daughter, who is of or
-- over the age of 18 years, of the person; or (d) a parent of the person; or (e) a brother or sister, who is of or over the
-- age of 18 years, of the person; or (f) an executor named in the will of the person or a person who, immediately before
-- the death, was a personal representative of the person; or (g) any person nominated by the person to be contacted in an
-- emergency." The list is "unless otherwise prescribed"; the Coroners Regulations 1997 prescribe nothing otherwise, so the
-- list applies as written.
DECLARE `Relationship to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `partner in a marriage-like relationship`
    `son or daughter`
    `parent`
    `brother or sister`
    `other relative or no relation`

DECLARE Kin HAS
    `relationship to the deceased` IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
    `lived with the deceased immediately before death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `aged 18 or over` IS A BOOLEAN
    `named executor in the will, or was the personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `nominated by the deceased as the emergency contact` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A person's place in the s 37(5) list: 1 for (a) to 7 for (g); 99 means not on the list. A person who fits two
-- paragraphs takes the higher place.
@export What is my place in the order of next of kin under s 37(5) (1 is first; 99 means not on the list)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Kin @desc Your relationship to the deceased
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my place in the order of next of kin` `me` IS
    BRANCH
      IF     `me`'s `lived with the deceased immediately before death`
         AND (   `me`'s `relationship to the deceased` EQUALS `spouse`
              OR (`me`'s `relationship to the deceased` EQUALS `partner in a marriage-like relationship` AND `me`'s `aged 18 or over`))
        THEN 1
      IF `me`'s `relationship to the deceased` EQUALS `spouse`
        THEN 2
      IF `me`'s `relationship to the deceased` EQUALS `son or daughter` AND `me`'s `aged 18 or over`
        THEN 3
      IF `me`'s `relationship to the deceased` EQUALS `parent`
        THEN 4
      IF `me`'s `relationship to the deceased` EQUALS `brother or sister` AND `me`'s `aged 18 or over`
        THEN 5
      IF `me`'s `named executor in the will, or was the personal representative`
        THEN 6
      IF `me`'s `nominated by the deceased as the emergency contact`
        THEN 7
      OTHERWISE 99

-- "Any of the deceased person's next of kin under section 37(5)" (ss 20, 25(4), 30(2)) is read as anyone on the s 37(5)
-- list, not only the senior next of kin (an inference).
@export Am I one of the deceased's next of kin under s 37(5)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Kin @desc Your relationship to the deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I one of the next of kin` `me` IF
    `What is my place in the order of next of kin` `me` LESS THAN 99

-- "The first person who is available": the text does not say who comes first between two available people in the same
-- paragraph (two adult children, say). That case is returned as such, not resolved.
DECLARE `Whether I am the senior next of kin` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am the senior next of kin`
    `I share the first place with another available person; s 37(5) does not say who goes first`
    `no: someone available ranks ahead of me, or I am not on the list`

@export Am I the senior next of kin (Coroners Act 1996 (WA) s 37(5))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Kin @desc Your relationship to the deceased
      `the best place of anyone else available` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest place (1 to 7) held by anyone else who is available; 99 if no one else on the list is available
GIVETH A `Whether I am the senior next of kin`
DECIDE `Am I the senior next of kin` `me` `the best place of anyone else available` IS
    BRANCH
      IF `What is my place in the order of next of kin` `me` EQUALS 99
        THEN `no: someone available ranks ahead of me, or I am not on the list`
      IF `What is my place in the order of next of kin` `me` LESS THAN `the best place of anyone else available`
        THEN `yes: I am the senior next of kin`
      IF `What is my place in the order of next of kin` `me` EQUALS `the best place of anyone else available`
        THEN `I share the first place with another available person; s 37(5) does not say who goes first`
      OTHERWISE `no: someone available ranks ahead of me, or I am not on the list`

§§ `20, 25(4), 26A, 30(2), 35 -- what the family must be told and allowed`

-- s 20(1): "A coroner who has jurisdiction to investigate a death must, as soon as practicable after assuming that
-- jurisdiction, provide to any of the deceased person's next of kin under section 37(5)" the information in (a)-(j): that
-- the body is under the coroner's control, a post mortem is likely, the right to view and touch the body, the right to have
-- a doctor present at the post mortem, the right to object to it or to ask for one, tissue retention, how to object, and
-- counselling. (2): "in writing, where practicable, and in a language and form likely to be understood".
@export Must the coroner tell me, in writing where practicable, about the body, the post mortem and my rights (s 20)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Kin @desc Your relationship to the deceased
      `the death` IS A Death @desc How and where the person died
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the coroner give me the section 20 information` `me` `the death` IF
        `Is this a reportable death` `the death`
    AND `Am I one of the next of kin` `me`

-- s 30(2): "While a body is under the control of the coroner investigating the death, the coroner is to ensure that any of
-- the deceased person's next of kin under section 37(5) who wish to view the body are permitted to do so and any of those
-- persons who wish to touch the body are permitted to do so, unless the coroner determines that it is undesirable or
-- dangerous to do so." s 20(1)(c) ties the "unless" to touching; (f) states the right to view with no qualification. The
-- "unless" is read as qualifying touching only (an inference).
@export While the coroner holds the body, may I view it (s 30(2), s 20(1)(f))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Kin @desc Your relationship to the deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I view the body` `me` IF
    `Am I one of the next of kin` `me`

@export While the coroner holds the body, may I touch it (s 30(2), s 20(1)(c))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Kin @desc Your relationship to the deceased
      `the coroner has determined that touching is undesirable or dangerous (coroner)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the coroner has determined that touching the body is undesirable or dangerous
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I touch the body` `me` `the coroner has determined that touching is undesirable or dangerous (coroner)` IF
        `Am I one of the next of kin` `me`
    AND (NOT `the coroner has determined that touching is undesirable or dangerous (coroner)`)

-- s 35: "If the senior next of kin of the deceased asks a coroner to allow a doctor chosen by the senior next of kin to be
-- present at a post mortem examination, the coroner is to allow that doctor to be present and is to ensure that the doctor
-- is informed as to the time and place".
@export Must the coroner let a doctor I choose attend the post mortem (s 35)?
GIVEN `I am the senior next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the senior next of kin
      `I have asked the coroner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have asked the coroner to allow your doctor to be present
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my doctor be allowed at the post mortem` `I am the senior next of kin` `I have asked the coroner` IF
    `I am the senior next of kin` AND `I have asked the coroner`

-- s 25(4): "Where a post mortem examination is held as part of the investigation of a death and a finding has not been made
-- within 21 days after that post mortem examination, then the coroner must provide written information on that examination
-- to any of the next of kin under section 37(5), unless it is not practicable to do so." Read as arising once more than 21
-- days have passed without a finding.
@export Must the coroner give me written information on the post mortem (s 25(4))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Kin @desc Your relationship to the deceased
      `days since the post mortem` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the post mortem examination
      `the coroner has made a finding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the coroner has made a finding
      `it is not practicable (coroner)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is not practicable for the coroner to give the information
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the coroner give me written information on the post mortem` `me` `days since the post mortem` `the coroner has made a finding` `it is not practicable (coroner)` IF
        `Am I one of the next of kin` `me`
    AND `days since the post mortem` GREATER THAN 21
    AND (NOT `the coroner has made a finding`)
    AND (NOT `it is not practicable (coroner)`)

-- s 26A: "If the senior next of kin of a deceased person asks a coroner for access to evidence obtained for the purpose of
-- investigating the death, the coroner is to give that person access to that evidence, unless the coroner believes it is
-- not desirable or practicable to do so."
@export Must the coroner give me access to the evidence gathered in the investigation (s 26A)?
GIVEN `I am the senior next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the senior next of kin
      `the coroner believes it not desirable or practicable (coroner)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the coroner believes access is not desirable or practicable
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the coroner give me access to the evidence` `I am the senior next of kin` `the coroner believes it not desirable or practicable (coroner)` IF
    `I am the senior next of kin` AND (NOT `the coroner believes it not desirable or practicable (coroner)`)

§§ `37 -- objecting to a post mortem`

-- s 37(1): "If the senior next of kin ... asks a coroner not to direct a post mortem examination but the coroner decides that
-- a post mortem examination is necessary, the coroner must immediately give notice in writing to the senior next of kin".
-- (2): "Unless the coroner believes that a post mortem examination needs to be performed immediately it must not be
-- performed if a request has been made under subsection (1) until 2 clear working days after the senior next of kin has been
-- given notice of the decision or until after the end of any extension of time granted by the Supreme Court". (2a): the
-- coroner may direct a post mortem if the request is withdrawn. (4): the Supreme Court may order that none be performed.
-- Nothing in s 37 holds the post mortem back merely because an application to the Supreme Court has been lodged in time.
-- "Clear working days" are counted as whole working days that have passed since notice.
@export Can the post mortem go ahead despite my objection as senior next of kin (s 37(1)-(4))?
GIVEN `clear working days since I was given notice of the decision` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole working days that have passed since you were given the coroner's written notice that a post mortem is necessary
      `the coroner believes it must be performed immediately (coroner)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the coroner believes the post mortem must be performed immediately
      `an extension granted by the Supreme Court is still running` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has granted an extension of time that has not ended
      `the Supreme Court has ordered no post mortem` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has ordered that no post mortem be performed
      `I have withdrawn my objection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have withdrawn your request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the post mortem go ahead despite my objection` `clear working days since I was given notice of the decision` `the coroner believes it must be performed immediately (coroner)` `an extension granted by the Supreme Court is still running` `the Supreme Court has ordered no post mortem` `I have withdrawn my objection` IF
        (NOT `the Supreme Court has ordered no post mortem`)
    AND (   `I have withdrawn my objection`
         OR `the coroner believes it must be performed immediately (coroner)`
         OR (    `clear working days since I was given notice of the decision` AT LEAST 2
             AND (NOT `an extension granted by the Supreme Court is still running`)))

-- s 37(3): "Within 2 clear working days after receiving notice of the decision, or before the end of any extension of time
-- granted by the Supreme Court, the senior next of kin may apply to the Supreme Court for an order that no post mortem
-- examination be performed." (3a): an extension only "if the post mortem examination has not been performed".
@export May I still apply to the Supreme Court to stop the post mortem (s 37(3))?
GIVEN `clear working days since I received notice of the decision` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole working days that have passed since you received the coroner's notice
      `an extension granted by the Supreme Court is still running` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has granted an extension of time that has not ended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the Supreme Court to stop the post mortem` `clear working days since I received notice of the decision` `an extension granted by the Supreme Court is still running` IF
        `clear working days since I received notice of the decision` LESS THAN 2
    OR  `an extension granted by the Supreme Court is still running`

§§ `29, 30, 36(3) -- when the body is released`

-- s 30(1): "If a reportable death occurs and the body is in Western Australia, the body is under the control of the coroner
-- investigating the death ... until the coroner has issued a certificate under section 29(1)." s 29(1): the coroner "must
-- issue as soon as reasonably possible a certificate in the prescribed form permitting burial, cremation or other disposal
-- of the body or any parts of the body".
DECLARE `Whether the coroner holds the body` IS ONE OF
    `not held by the coroner: the Coroners Act does not hold it back`
    `held by the coroner until the s 29 certificate is issued (s 30(1))`
    `released: the s 29 certificate permits burial, cremation or other disposal`

@export Does the coroner hold the body, or may we have it for the funeral (ss 29(1), 30(1))?
GIVEN `the death` IS A Death @desc How and where the person died, and where the body is
      `the coroner has issued the s 29 certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the coroner has issued the certificate permitting burial, cremation or other disposal
GIVETH A `Whether the coroner holds the body`
DECIDE `Does the coroner hold the body` `the death` `the coroner has issued the s 29 certificate` IS
    BRANCH
      IF (NOT `Is this a reportable death` `the death`) OR (NOT `the death`'s `the body is in Western Australia`)
        THEN `not held by the coroner: the Coroners Act does not hold it back`
      IF `the coroner has issued the s 29 certificate`
        THEN `released: the s 29 certificate permits burial, cremation or other disposal`
      OTHERWISE `held by the coroner until the s 29 certificate is issued (s 30(1))`

-- s 29(2): the certificate "must not be issued until -- (a) an application made under section 36(3) is disposed of; or (b)
-- the time specified in section 36(3) for making an application has expired; or (c) if the coroner ... has notice that an
-- application has been made under section 36(3a) for an extension of time, the application is disposed of or any extension
-- of time granted under section 36(3a) has expired." (3): "If the Supreme Court makes an order under section 36(4) a
-- coroner, other than the State Coroner, must not issue a certificate". s 36(3): a person refused a post mortem may apply to
-- the Supreme Court "within 2 clear working days after receiving notice of a refusal".
DECLARE `Request by anyone for a post mortem` IS ONE OF
    `no one's request for a post mortem has been refused`
    `a request was refused and the 2 clear working days to apply to the Supreme Court are running`
    `the time to apply has passed with no application`
    `an application to the Supreme Court, or for an extension, is pending or an extension is running`
    `the application has been disposed of without an order`
    `the Supreme Court has ordered a post mortem (s 36(4))`

DECLARE `When the disposal certificate can issue` IS ONE OF
    `now: the coroner must issue it as soon as reasonably possible (s 29(1))`
    `not yet: the s 36 application or the time for it must run out first (s 29(2))`
    `only the State Coroner may issue it, after the ordered post mortem (ss 29(3), 36(4))`

@export When can the coroner issue the certificate releasing the body for burial or cremation (s 29)?
GIVEN `the request` IS A `Request by anyone for a post mortem` @desc Where any request by anyone for a post mortem stands
GIVETH A `When the disposal certificate can issue`
DECIDE `When can the disposal certificate issue` `the request` IS
    CONSIDER `the request`
      WHEN `a request was refused and the 2 clear working days to apply to the Supreme Court are running`
        THEN `not yet: the s 36 application or the time for it must run out first (s 29(2))`
      WHEN `an application to the Supreme Court, or for an extension, is pending or an extension is running`
        THEN `not yet: the s 36 application or the time for it must run out first (s 29(2))`
      WHEN `the Supreme Court has ordered a post mortem (s 36(4))`
        THEN `only the State Coroner may issue it, after the ordered post mortem (ss 29(3), 36(4))`
      OTHERWISE `now: the coroner must issue it as soon as reasonably possible (s 29(1))`

§§ `44, reg 17 -- may I take part in the inquest`

-- s 44(1): "An interested person may appear, or be represented by a legal practitioner, at an inquest and examine or
-- crossexamine witnesses." (2): "Before a coroner makes any finding adverse to the interests of an interested person, that
-- person must be given the opportunity to present submissions". (3): "There may be prescribed a list of persons who are
-- interested persons for the purpose of this section, but such a list is not a conclusive list of interested persons."
-- Coroners Regulations 1997 reg 17: "The following persons are interested persons for the purposes of section 44(3) of the
-- Act -- (a) a spouse, de facto partner, child, parent or other personal representative of the deceased person; (b) any of
-- the deceased person's next of kin under section 37(5) of the Act; (c) a beneficiary under a policy of insurance issued on
-- the life of the deceased person; ..." Paragraphs (d)-(g) (the insurer, a person whose act may have caused the death, a
-- union's appointee, the Commissioner of Police) are not the family and are not encoded. "De facto partner" is a borrowed
-- term and is read as the relationship `partner in a marriage-like relationship` (an inference). "Child" in (a) has no age
-- limit, unlike "son or daughter ... of or over the age of 18" in s 37(5)(c).
DECLARE `Whether I am an interested person` IS ONE OF
    `yes: on the prescribed list as spouse, de facto partner, child, parent or personal representative (reg 17(a))`
    `yes: on the prescribed list as one of the next of kin under s 37(5) (reg 17(b))`
    `yes: on the prescribed list as a beneficiary of insurance on the deceased's life (reg 17(c))`
    `not on the prescribed list; the list is not conclusive (s 44(3)), so it is for the coroner`

GIVEN `me` IS A Kin
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am within regulation 17(a)` `me` IF
        `me`'s `relationship to the deceased` EQUALS `spouse`
    OR  `me`'s `relationship to the deceased` EQUALS `partner in a marriage-like relationship`
    OR  `me`'s `relationship to the deceased` EQUALS `son or daughter`
    OR  `me`'s `relationship to the deceased` EQUALS `parent`
    OR  `me`'s `named executor in the will, or was the personal representative`

@export Am I an interested person who may appear at the inquest, be represented and question witnesses (Coroners Act 1996 (WA) s 44; Coroners Regulations 1997 reg 17)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Kin @desc Your relationship to the deceased
      `I am a beneficiary of insurance on the deceased's life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a beneficiary under a policy of insurance issued on the deceased's life
GIVETH A `Whether I am an interested person`
DECIDE `Am I an interested person at the inquest` `me` `I am a beneficiary of insurance on the deceased's life` IS
    BRANCH
      IF `I am within regulation 17(a)` `me`
        THEN `yes: on the prescribed list as spouse, de facto partner, child, parent or personal representative (reg 17(a))`
      IF `Am I one of the next of kin` `me`
        THEN `yes: on the prescribed list as one of the next of kin under s 37(5) (reg 17(b))`
      IF `I am a beneficiary of insurance on the deceased's life`
        THEN `yes: on the prescribed list as a beneficiary of insurance on the deceased's life (reg 17(c))`
      OTHERWISE `not on the prescribed list; the list is not conclusive (s 44(3)), so it is for the coroner`

§§ `regs 22, 22A, 23B, Schedule 3 item 2 -- what I pay for copies of the record of investigation`

-- Schedule 3 item 2, "Copy of record of investigation into a death -- (a) for 1 copy on the request of a person who is an
-- interested person under regulation 17(a) or (b): No fee [both columns]; (b) for each additional copy on the request of a
-- person who is an interested person under regulation 17(a) or (b) -- for each page or part of a page: 2.25 [Column A], 0.70
-- [Column B]; (c) for each copy on the request of any other person -- for each page or part of a page: 2.25, 0.70".
-- reg 22(2): Column A is the fee for "an individual who is not an eligible individual", Column B for "an eligible
-- individual". reg 22A: no fee if "(a) a written law provides that the person is not required to pay a fee in respect of a
-- matter of that type; or (b) the person has not reached 18 years of age on the day the fee would otherwise be payable".
-- reg 23B(2): an eligible individual holds a Centrelink health care, health benefit, pensioner concession or Commonwealth
-- seniors health card (or another card certifying Commonwealth health concessions), receives youth training allowance,
-- AUSTUDY or ABSTUDY, has legal aid for the proceedings, or has been directed to be one under reg 23D (financial hardship or
-- the interests of justice); which of these applies is asked as one fact. reg 22A(a) (another written law) is not asked.
-- reg 23A's waiver covers items 1 and 4 only, not item 2.
`the item 2 fee per page` MEANS 2.25
`the item 2 fee per page for an eligible individual` MEANS 0.70

@export How much must I pay for copies of the coroner's record of investigation into the death (Coroners Regulations 1997 regs 22, 22A, 23B, Schedule 3 item 2)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Kin @desc Your relationship to the deceased
      `copies I ask for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many copies of the record you are asking for now
      `pages in the record` IS A NUMBER @desc Pages in one copy of the record (a part page counts as a page)
      `I have already had my free copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already been given the one copy that is free
      `I am an eligible individual under reg 23B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a Centrelink concession or health card, receive youth allowance, AUSTUDY or ABSTUDY, have legal aid for the proceedings, or have been directed to be an eligible individual
      `I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18 on the day the fee would be payable
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much do I pay for copies of the record` `me` `copies I ask for` `pages in the record` `I have already had my free copy` `I am an eligible individual under reg 23B` `I am under 18` IS
    IF `I am under 18`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `copies charged` TIMES `pages in the record` TIMES `the page rate`
    WHERE
      `I am within item 2(a) and (b)` MEANS `I am within regulation 17(a)` `me` OR `Am I one of the next of kin` `me`
      `copies charged` MEANS
          IF `I am within item 2(a) and (b)` AND (NOT `I have already had my free copy`) AND `copies I ask for` AT LEAST 1
          THEN `copies I ask for` MINUS 1
          ELSE `copies I ask for`
      `the page rate` MEANS
          IF `I am an eligible individual under reg 23B`
          THEN `the item 2 fee per page for an eligible individual`
          ELSE `the item 2 fee per page`
